<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-229 P3.8 (bead nexus-p2m1x.28): a partial UNIQUE index on the live collection tuple.

    THE INDEX. nexus.catalog_collections gets
        UNIQUE (tenant_id, content_type, owner_id, embedding_model, model_version)
        WHERE superseded_by = '' AND lifecycle_state <> 'quarantine'
    The predicate is exactly the candidate set of CatalogRepository.collectionForTuple, so a tuple can never have two
    answers at the same model_version: a dormant or disputed row still holds its tuple (it is what the lookup
    answers), a quarantine sibling and a superseded row do not. model_version is in the key so a same-model re-embed
    target (registered live while its source still is, at a higher version) or a revive is never refused. The mint
    becomes INSERT ... ON CONFLICT ... DO NOTHING plus a re-read, which is race-safe with no advisory lock. The
    design of record is T2 nexus_rdr/229-p3.8-design-gate-v2-2026-11-21, accepted by Sam 2026-11-21 (T2
    nexus/sam-ruling-rdr229-p38-design-gate-v2-2026-11-21). Reversible: drop the index.

    THE INDEX WAITS (RDR-246, "Finishing a move"). On the managed tenant gate-xr789 the curator's two docs
    collections share one tuple until the re-own move of the P3 plan (marlowe's, label
    'rdr229-reown-repo-stems-from-curator') has run, and a UNIQUE index cannot be built over a duplicate. The changeset
    is therefore a preCondition with onFail="CONTINUE" and onError="CONTINUE", on purpose:
      - never HALT: a boot-time halt crash-loops an install (the nexus-lgdel.l1 no-wedge directive);
      - never MARK_RAN: that would record the changeset as run and stop it being retried. CONTINUE skips the
        changeset WITHOUT recording it, so every boot re-evaluates it and the index lands the first boot both
        conditions hold: (a) the nexus.data_moves row with that label has completed_at set, and (b)
        nexus.catalog_collection_tuple_duplicates_unscoped() returns 0.
    The move is named by its LABEL, not by a changeset id: the move is registered by an engine boot, not by this
    file. A fresh install therefore takes two boots: boot 1's migration runs before the move exists (skipped), the
    engine then registers it and its worker completes it (nothing to move), and boot 2 applies the index.
    The two conditions are ONE sqlCheck on purpose: the CASE reaches the counter only when the move has completed, so a
    boot that is still waiting for the move reads no row of the registry at all; nothing in Liquibase promises the order
    of two nested checks.

    THE COUNTER IS A PLAIN, READ-ONLY SQL FUNCTION AND TAKES NO TABLE LOCK BEYOND A READ. nexus.catalog_collections is
    FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY with the policy `tenant_id = current_setting('nexus.tenant', true)` (catalog-001-5), and the
    migration role owns the table with no BYPASSRLS (the nexus-1wjmq class, catalog-013-1b's header). With no tenant GUC
    set, a count by that role sees ZERO rows on every tenant unless a policy lets it read them. RDR-229 D2 ships that
    policy as catalog_collections_owner_read (FOR SELECT TO CURRENT_USER USING (true), changeset
    vectors-065-catalog-collections-owner-read, with the guard that skips it where a role subject to row-level security
    would inherit it). The counter (collections-001-1) is a SECURITY INVOKER function that runs as the migration role and
    reads every tenant's rows through that policy. THIS FILE CREATES NO POLICY AND CHANGES NO TABLE SETTING: lifting the
    table's FORCE flag for a count would take a lock that blocks every reader of the registry for the length of a count,
    on every boot, and a boot in the cloud must never do that.
    Where the policy is absent (D2 not yet applied, or its guard skipped it in a single-role install) the counter reads
    no row and answers 0. That is safe, not silent: the index build below then refuses on a real duplicate, the changeset
    is skipped unrecorded and retried at the next boot, and nx doctor names the duplicate from the catalog's own listing.

    THE GUARD CANNOT HALT A BOOT. A sqlCheck that THROWS is an error, not a failed check, and onError="CONTINUE" turns it
    into the same skip (a migration role with no privilege on the table is refused at the counter this way). The body is a single CREATE UNIQUE INDEX with failOnError="false": a duplicate that lands between
    the precondition and the body, or a duplicate the counter could not see, makes the index build raise, Liquibase rolls the body back, logs it, and writes NO DATABASECHANGELOG row
    (MarkChangeSetRanGenerator refuses a FAILED changeset), so it is retried at the next boot exactly like a precondition
    skip. The build reads the heap and is not subject to RLS, so it sees every tenant's rows. GET /v1/status reports
    collection_tuple_index_present, and nx doctor names a duplicate that holds the index back, and an index that waits for
    no reason it can name.

    LOCKS. The counter reads (ACCESS SHARE). The index build takes SHARE on nexus.catalog_collections only, for one build
    of a registry of hundreds of rows. Neither names a chunk table, a chunk leaf or the index builder, so
    tests/test_changelog_continue_precondition_chunks_lint.py allows the CONTINUE changeset and SchemaMigrator keeps a
    running per-collection index build through it. No statement in this file asks for ACCESS EXCLUSIVE
    (CollectionTupleUniqueIndexLiquibaseTest holds ACCESS SHARE on the registry for a whole walk and requires it to finish).

    DATA EFFECT: none. collections-001-1 creates a function and no row is read or written by a changeset; collections-001-2
    builds an index and writes no row.

    Placed after identity-005 and before the runAlways grants blocks (the D0.1 late-append convention).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset 1: the guard's duplicate counter ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="collections-001-1" author="nexus-p2m1x.28">
        <comment>Create nexus.catalog_collection_tuple_duplicates_unscoped(): the number of live tuples (tenant_id, content_type, owner_id, embedding_model, model_version, over rows with superseded_by = '' and lifecycle_state other than quarantine, the candidate set of collectionForTuple) that more than one row of nexus.catalog_collections holds. A plain read-only SECURITY INVOKER SQL function: it runs as the migration role and reads every tenant's rows through RDR-229 D2's owner-read policy catalog_collections_owner_read (changeset vectors-065); it changes no table setting and takes no lock beyond a read. Where that policy is absent it reads no row and answers 0. Used by collections-001-2's precondition. DATA EFFECT: none (a function is created; no row is read or written by the changeset).</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION nexus.catalog_collection_tuple_duplicates_unscoped() RETURNS bigint
LANGUAGE sql STABLE SECURITY INVOKER
AS $fn$
    SELECT count(*) FROM (
        SELECT 1
          FROM nexus.catalog_collections
         WHERE superseded_by = '' AND lifecycle_state &lt;&gt; 'quarantine'
         GROUP BY tenant_id, content_type, owner_id, embedding_model, model_version
        HAVING count(*) &gt; 1
    ) d
$fn$;

REVOKE ALL ON FUNCTION nexus.catalog_collection_tuple_duplicates_unscoped() FROM PUBLIC;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS nexus.catalog_collection_tuple_duplicates_unscoped();
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- ── Changeset 2: the index, once the move has completed and no duplicate is left ──────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="collections-001-2" author="nexus-p2m1x.28" failOnError="false">
        <preConditions onFail="CONTINUE" onError="CONTINUE">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">SELECT CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM nexus.data_moves WHERE label = 'rdr229-reown-repo-stems-from-curator' AND completed_at IS NOT NULL) THEN nexus.catalog_collection_tuple_duplicates_unscoped() ELSE -1 END</sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>Create the partial UNIQUE index catalog_collections_live_tuple_uq on nexus.catalog_collections (tenant_id, content_type, owner_id, embedding_model, model_version) WHERE superseded_by = '' AND lifecycle_state is not quarantine (the candidate set of collectionForTuple). Guarded by a preCondition with onFail="CONTINUE" onError="CONTINUE": the nexus.data_moves row labelled rdr229-reown-repo-stems-from-curator has completed_at set (the re-own move of RDR-229 P3), and nexus.catalog_collection_tuple_duplicates_unscoped() is 0 (one sqlCheck: the counter is reached only once the move has completed). Otherwise the changeset is skipped, boot continues, and the changeset is NOT recorded as run (a precondition skip records nothing, and a failed build with failOnError="false" is not recorded either), so it is retried at every boot, never HALT and never MARK_RAN. DATA EFFECT: none; an index is built and no row is read for writing or written.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX catalog_collections_live_tuple_uq
    ON nexus.catalog_collections (tenant_id, content_type, owner_id, embedding_model, model_version)
    WHERE superseded_by = '' AND lifecycle_state &lt;&gt; 'quarantine';
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            DROP INDEX IF EXISTS nexus.catalog_collections_live_tuple_uq;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
